q
1 0 0 1 57.02362 353.7008 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 34.5 Tm 15 TL /F1 10.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (MyISAM is not suitable for a payment transaction store because it does not provide the transaction and) Tj T* (crash-recovery guarantees expected for this type of workload. The specific alternative is ) Tj /F2 10.5 Tf (InnoDB) Tj /F1 10.5 Tf (, which) Tj T* (supports transactions, row-level locking and crash recovery.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 57.02362 263.7008 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 67.8 Tm /F2 12.2 Tf 16 TL (Q24. The bank has 40 million rows in account_txn and growing by 2 million a) Tj T* (month. The branch operations team wants a screen showing every transaction for) Tj T* (an account, and the risk team wants monthly totals across all accounts. Explain) Tj T* (why one database design cannot serve both well, and describe the two-system) Tj T* (arrangement.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 57.02362 182.7008 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 64.5 Tm 15 TL /F1 10.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (The account screen needs fast selective queries for day-to-day operations, while monthly totals require) Tj T* (large scans and aggregations across historical data. Running both workloads on the same system can) Tj T* (make the operational screen slower. I would keep the operational database for transactions and use a) Tj T* (separate data warehouse/reporting system for analytics. In this programme, Module 10 builds) Tj T* /F2 10.5 Tf (ICICIBankDW) Tj /F1 10.5 Tf ( for the warehouse side.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 57.02362 124.7008 cm
q
