BT 1 0 0 1 0 35.8 Tm /F2 12.2 Tf 16 TL -0.147257 Tw (Q27. A new joiner argues that check constraints such as balance >= 0 belong in the) Tj T* 0 Tw (application, not the database. Give two arguments for keeping the rule in the) Tj T* (database, and one situation where the application layer is the right place.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 57.02362 580.7008 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 49.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL (First, a database constraint protects the rule regardless of which application or job changes the data.) Tj T* (Second, it keeps the basic data-integrity rule in one central place and prevents invalid balances from) Tj T* (being stored. The application layer is better for complex workflow rules that depend on external) Tj T* (services, user interaction or broader business decisions.) Tj T* ET
